maluos-firstboot (0.1.9) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The enroll section of firstboot.yaml (Phase 11 slice 2; written by the
    MaluOS installer from the install plan): kind office runs `maluctl office
    enroll URL --code CODE --name NAME --owner USER` after provisioning and
    blanks the one-time code in the file once used; kind estate reports that
    estate enrolment is not available on this release (Phase 13 slice 1) and
    leaves the key. The outcome is in the state file; `maluctl status` (and
    `maluctl firstboot status`) show an enrolment line.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0000

maluos-firstboot (0.1.8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * maluctl update auto (Phase 12 slice 7, the Upgrade Manager's switches):
    automatic updates on|off, set security|maluos|mozilla on|off, reboot
    on|off [--at HH:MM]. Written as two drop-ins beside the shipped policy
    (53maluos-auto, 54maluos-origins) and a state file naming who changed
    what and when; the policy file is never edited and every switch at its
    default removes the drop-ins. `status` reports an off switch with its
    date and author. A polkit action (com.maluos.admin, for pkexec maluctl,
    administrator authentication kept per session) lets the desktop call
    `pkexec maluctl update auto …`.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:35:00 +0000

